<title>UK: John Lewis weekly UK store sales up 14.0%.</title>
<headline>John Lewis weekly UK store sales up 14.0%.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The John Lewis Partnership said on Friday its UK department store sales for the week to September 14 were up 14.0 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>For the seven weeks to September 14, department store sales were up 16.8 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Total sales, including those from the Waitrose supermarket chain, rose 12.4 percent year-on-year. For the seven-week period, sales were up 12.9 percent.</p>
<p>-- Michael Peacock, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
